          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How does the C 1650 compare to the C 990?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              They share the same 3.0 CHP motor and 0-10% incline range,
              but the C 1650 has a longer 20 x 60-inch deck versus the C
              990's 20 x 55-inch deck, and a larger 10-inch touchscreen
              instead of 7 inches. For roughly $300 more, the C 1650 is the
              better choice for anyone who runs regularly rather than only
              walks.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is the C 1650 good for running, or just walking?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              It handles walking, incline walking, and moderate jogging
              comfortably thanks to its 60-inch deck length, which matches
              NordicTrack's Commercial-series machines. The 3.0 CHP motor
              is still a step below the Commercial line's 3.75 CHP, so
              serious daily runners logging faster-paced miles will feel
              more headroom on a Commercial 1750, but casual and moderate
              runners will be well served here.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Should I buy the C 1650 or save more for the Commercial 1750?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              The Commercial 1750 has a stronger 3.75 CHP motor, a wider
              22-inch deck, and a larger touchscreen for roughly $500 more.
              If your budget realistically stops at the C 1650, you're
              still getting a 60-inch deck length and a genuine NordicTrack
              and iFit experience; the Commercial 1750 is worth the jump
              specifically for runners who want more width and motor
              headroom.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Do I have to pay for iFit to use the C 1650?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              The treadmill runs without an active subscription, but
              automatic incline adjustments during trainer-led workouts and
              the full workout library require iFit. It ships with a
              one-year membership included, giving you time to decide
              whether the coached format is worth continuing to pay for
              afterward.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is the 10-inch screen a meaningful upgrade over the C 990's 7-inch screen?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              Yes, noticeably. The larger display makes trail video and
              workout content feel closer to watching on a small tablet
              than the C 990's more phone-sized 7-inch screen. Reading
              stats at a glance during faster-paced workouts is easier
              too, since text and numbers render larger without feeling
              cramped.
            </p>
